    "body": "DUNCAN_PRIME_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_R01\n\nEXACT_HEAD = `2955467657274200b6b25b4f6e2d0eba34a443bd`\nBASE = `main@b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nRESULT = `FAIL_CLOSED / NOT READY FOR MERGE OR LIVE PROOF`\nPRODUCTION_ACTIVE = NO\nMERGE = NO\n\nIndependent read of the exact two-file diff confirms the intended boundary is narrow: one protected `issue_comment.created` caller for PR #111, OWNER actor + R03 marker admission, durable `write_and_verify` before execution, separate read-only revalidation, then the existing compiled LESTER workflow consuming only revalidated bindings. No repository_dispatch/finalize/auto-merge path is added. `hq-scope-guard` and `hq-control-tower-integrity` are green; actionlint and zizmor are green.\n\nFIRST EXACT FAILURE:\n- `hq-validate` run `33542773065` = FAILURE.\n- `hq-schema` job `99972845155`: `scripts/hq_validate.py` PASS, full unittest = 285 tests / 1 failure.\n- failing test: `R03LesterLiveCallerTests.test_separate_read_only_revalidation_is_mandatory_before_lester`.\n- exact mismatch: test asserts the literal escaped text `permissions:\\\\n ...`, while the workflow contains real YAML newlines.\n- commit `2955467657274200b6b25b4f6e2d0eba34a443bd` specifically repaired revalidation outputs from literal `\\\\n` emission to real newline emission, but the permission assertion remained on the old escaped-text expectation.\n\nTherefore the current CI failure at this boundary is a stale test expectation, not evidence that the workflow lacks read-only revalidation permissions. It still blocks PASS on this exact HEAD.\n\nSECOND CI BLOCKER:\n- `oss-security` run `33542773080` = FAILURE at Gitleaks.\n- the three `generic-api-key` findings are in pre-existing history (`hq/archive-v1/...`, `reference_analysis.py`, `ZORR_HYPERSPEED_RUN_PIPELINE_STUDY_R01.md`) and are outside #253's changed files. This review does NOT classify them as real secrets, but required security CI is objectively not green.\n\nPR has no submitted independent GitHub reviews/comments before this record.\n\nNEXT LEGAL STEP:\n1. LESTER makes the smallest test-only repair for the stale newline expectation; do not change the proven caller behavior to satisfy the test.\n2. Resolve/reuse the already-established handling for the three historical Gitleaks findings; do not weaken full-history secret scanning generically.\n3. Fresh CI on the new exact HEAD.\n4. DUNCAN independent re-review of that exact HEAD.\n5. Only after fresh green required evidence: decide merge gate; bounded live proof remains post-merge/approval and is not authorized by this review.",
